% -e shows each component's plans as it is planned, then each query's.  The
% recursive rule scans edge, which is complete, and looks up path, which is
% still being derived; its delta variant scans the delta and looks edge up by
% the column the delta bound.  The second query runs against the program the
% first materialized, so it shows only its own plan, and looks path up by the
% other column, through an index built for it.

edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
edge(c, d).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- edge(X, Y), path(Y, Z).

path(a, X)?
path(X, d)?
